libdatachannel v0.24.5: under Mbed TLS, a DTLS fingerprint mismatch fails the handshake

NereusSDR for iOS patch, applied by ios/scripts/vendor-sources.sh libdatachannel
after it copies the pinned archive's files. MPL-2.0, like the file it changes;
the modified src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp is published with NereusSDR's source.

With Mbed TLS, DtlsTransport::CertificateCallback returned 1 when the peer's
certificate did not match the fingerprint in the remote description. Mbed TLS
passes a verify callback's nonzero return back from mbedtls_ssl_handshake, and a
positive value passed rtc::impl::mbedtls::check as success, so the handshake was
reported finished and the transport went to Connected. Media sessions still
failed afterwards (no keys were exported for SRTP), but a data-channel-only peer
would have opened its channels to a peer whose certificate did not match.

Following Mbed TLS's verify-callback convention (return 0 and set *flags, or
return a negative MBEDTLS_ERR_X509_* for a fatal error; the transport uses
MBEDTLS_SSL_VERIFY_OPTIONAL, under which flags alone are ignored), the callback
now sets MBEDTLS_X509_BADCERT_NOT_TRUSTED and returns
MBEDTLS_ERR_X509_CERT_VERIFY_FAILED, which Mbed TLS reports as a fatal error,
and the handshake loop treats any positive return as a failure.

Upstream master (checked 2026-09-24) still returns 1 here.

--- a/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp
+++ b/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp
@@ -550,6 +550,12 @@
 					                                });
 					return;
 				}
+
+				// A handshake step returns 0 on success and a negative code on error; any
+				// positive value is an error passed through from a callback, never success
+				if (ret > 0)
+					throw std::runtime_error("Handshake failed: unexpected return value " +
+					                         std::to_string(ret));
 
 				if (mbedtls::check(ret, "Handshake failed")) {
 					// RFC 8261: DTLS MUST support sending messages larger than the current path MTU
@@ -610,12 +616,18 @@
 }
 
 int DtlsTransport::CertificateCallback(void *ctx, mbedtls_x509_crt *crt, int /*depth*/,
-                                       uint32_t * /*flags*/) {
+                                       uint32_t *flags) {
 	auto this_ = static_cast<DtlsTransport *>(ctx);
 	string fingerprint = make_fingerprint(crt, this_->mFingerprintAlgorithm);
 	std::transform(fingerprint.begin(), fingerprint.end(), fingerprint.begin(),
 	               [](char c) { return char(std::toupper(c)); });
-	return this_->mVerifierCallback(fingerprint) ? 0 : 1;
+	if (this_->mVerifierCallback(fingerprint))
+		return 0;
+
+	// The authmode is MBEDTLS_SSL_VERIFY_OPTIONAL, under which flags alone are ignored, so the
+	// mismatch is reported as a fatal verification error, which aborts the handshake
+	*flags |= MBEDTLS_X509_BADCERT_NOT_TRUSTED;
+	return MBEDTLS_ERR_X509_CERT_VERIFY_FAILED;
 }
 
 void DtlsTransport::ExportKeysCallback(void *ctx, mbedtls_ssl_key_export_type /*type*/,
